om/sunshineluyao/ViRel-Budget/pull/1.patch", "merged_at": "2026-08-19T15:08:52Z"}, "body": "## What changed\n\n- correct repository, dataset, citation, author, and package metadata\n- distinguish prospective reliability evaluation from repeated-workload energy evidence\n- replace overstrong deployment and environmental language with bounded empirical claims\n- document dataset provenance, source-group isolation, zero-eligible-intervention handling, and artifact exclusions\n- pin CodeCarbon and external pruning repository revisions in the reproduction setup\n- clarify measurement assumptions and add an accurate open data and code statement\n\n## Why\n\nThe public artifact contained obsolete URLs, inconsistent author metadata, ambiguous use of \u201creplication,\u201d combined reliability/energy claims, and setup scripts that followed moving upstream repository heads. These revisions align the artifact with the camera-ready evidence boundary and improve reproducibility.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v` \u2014 29 tests passed\n- `python scripts/audit/verify_release.py` \u2014 passed\n- package CLI smoke check \u2014 passed\n- `pyproject.toml` and `CITATION.cff` parsing \u2014 passed\n- `bash -n scripts/setup/*.sh` \u2014 passed\n- `git diff --check` \u2014 passed", "closed_by": {"login": "sunshineluyao", "id": 48966917, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTY2OTE3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48966917?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunshineluyao", "html_url": "https://github.com/sunshineluyao", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunshineluyao/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunshineluyao/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunshineluyao/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunshineluyao/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sunshineluyao/subscriptions", "organ